Coursework outcomes
The coursework connects lecture theory with hands-on analysis of real grid data. Students learn to:

construct complete ML pipelines for power-system applications;
collect and preprocess irregularly sampled power-system data;
use zero-shot, autoregressive, and covariate-informed forecasting methods;
build DC power-flow measurement matrices;
perform weighted least-squares state estimation;
design chi-square bad-data detection with a controlled false-positive rate;
train classifiers for false-data injection attack detection; and
present algorithms, equations, and experimental methodology clearly.
